# Elrond, Moon-Reader: "Whenever you activate an ability of a creature, draw a card. This ability triggers only once each turn." A creature's mana ability counts (the
# ruling, CR 605.3): on turn 3 Bot1 taps Mox Sapphire (an artifact's ability: no trigger, the stack stays empty) and then Llanowar Elves, whose
# mana ability triggers it: one card drawn once the trigger resolves (the library goes from 18 to 17). On turn 5, a new turn, tapping the Elves draws again,
# and tapping the second Elves, also a creature, draws nothing more that turn: 16 and then still 16... the library counts show each step.

